Looking at the robot's path: it enters at row 2 moving east, hits the wall between Q2 and R2, turns right (south) to Q1, hits the bottom wall, turns right (west) to P1, hits the left wall, turns right (north) up column P to P4, hits the top wall, turns right (east) along row 4 to T4, hits the right wall, turns right (south) down column T to T1, hits the bottom wall, turns right (west) to S1, hits the wall between R1 and S1, turns right (north) up column S to S4, hits the top wall, turns right (east) to T4, then south to T1, then west to S1, then north again...

The robot enters a closed loop (S1 → S4 → T4 → T1 → S1 → ...) where at every wall it always has an open right turn. Therefore it never stops.

\boxed{E}
